---
source: crates/biome_yaml_analyze/tests/spec_tests.rs
expression: invalid.yaml
---
# Input
```yaml
# should generate diagnostics
person:
  name: John Doe
  age: 50
  name: Jane Doe

person2: { name: John, age: 50, name: Jane }

person3:
  name: John Doe
  "name": Jane Doe
  'name': Baby Doe

person4:
  name: John Doe
  age: 50
  name: Jane Doe
  age: 51

person5:
  # a comment before the first key
  name: John Doe
  age: 50
  # a comment before the duplicate key
  name: Jane Doe

person6: { name: John, age: 50, name: Jane } # trailing comment

parent:
  child:
    name: John Doe
    name: Jane Doe
  child: first
  child: second

# sequence of mappings, each with duplicates
people:
  - id: 1
    id: 2
  - name: a
    role: admin
    role: guest

# nested flow mappings, duplicates at both levels
config: { a: { x: 1, x: 2 }, a: 3 }

```

# Diagnostics
```
invalid.yaml:3:3 lint/nursery/noDuplicateMapKeys ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  × The key name was already declared.
  
    1 │ # should generate diagnostics
    2 │ person:
  > 3 │   name: John Doe
      │   ^^^^
    4 │   age: 50
    5 │   name: Jane Doe
  
  i This is where a duplicated key was declared again.
  
    3 │   name: John Doe
    4 │   age: 50
  > 5 │   name: Jane Doe
      │   ^^^^
    6 │ 
    7 │ person2: { name: John, age: 50, name: Jane }
  
  i Duplicate keys make the mapping ambiguous, and tools disagree on which value wins.
  
  i Remove or rename the duplicate keys.
  
  i This rule belongs to the nursery group, which means it is not yet stable and may change in the future. Visit https://biomejs.dev/linter/#nursery for more information.
  

```

